; Secret of Evermore: Casual Run -- version 2.0
; Chapter/area dialogue packed; compatible event wrappers consolidated.
; Expected built SHA-256: 718614572208aec79b28e2287a09369bd3c9b64d3b1e87a17be26b56ecbef0e6
; Address order is physical ROM order; dialogue passages retain chapter/area context.
; Every explicitly defined byte is written once. Unwritten bytes come from the clean base.
; Functional reservations include unchanged bytes; reservation does not mean free space.
; See Documentation/Helper_Consolidation_Functional_Regions.md and Helper_Consolidation.md for maintenance rules.
arch 65816
hirom

; FUNCTIONAL REGION DIRECTORY
; $C0FFC0-$C0FFFF: CARTRIDGE_HEADER
; Cartridge identity, mapper flags, checksum/complement, and vectors.
; Constraint: Preserve native vector entries and recalculate checksum after ROM changes.
; $C19903-$C199D7: NATIVE_MUSIC_POINTERS
; Native SPC song pointer table for IDs 0-70.
; Constraint: Native audio references this table; unchanged entries remain part of the audio system.
; $C45B9C-$C45BA4: ALCHEMY_EXPERIENCE_LEVEL_TABLE
; Nine byte-sized alchemy experience values indexed by level.
; Constraint: Keep all nine entries, including unchanged first/last entries. Native indexed reads and partial source writes must remain aligned.
; $C57410-$C574D9: SHARED_WEAPON_EXPERIENCE
; Same-family weapon experience sharing.
; Constraint: Preserve the equipment selector, scratch word and family branches; native callers use JSL and require RTL.
; $C574F0-$C5751D: CHARGE_DAMAGE_ARITHMETIC
; Charge-dependent attack arithmetic.
; Constraint: A/Y are 16-bit. Preserve thresholds, shifts, direct-page scratch and the CLC/SBC borrow behavior.
; $C57530-$C57575: ALCHEMY_SHARING_GROUPS
; 35 word-sized group tokens used by both sharing helpers.
; Constraint: Keep 70 bytes and the two-byte index stride, including inherited first low byte and zero group.
; $C57610-$C57669: SHARED_ALCHEMY_EXPERIENCE
; Alchemy progress gating and same-group scan.
; Constraint: Preserve the zero-progress path, WRAM data-bank contract, 35-entry scan and RTL stack balance.
; $C57680-$C576A3: ALCHEMY_GROUP_MEMBER_UPDATE
; Level-indexed experience update for one sharing-group member.
; Constraint: X is the alchemy word offset. Keep level-9 exclusion, 100-point threshold and indexed level/progress stores.
; $CC8BD3-$CC8E24: PROGRESSION_LOOKUP_DATA
; Experience and weapon progression lookup data.
; Constraint: These numeric table entries are not CPU instructions or addresses into expanded dialogue. Preserve the complete indexed allocation.
; $CEB678-$CEDF83: NATIVE_CHARACTER_RECORDS
; 142 native character/NPC records, 74 bytes each; enemy records begin at index 51.
; Constraint: Preserve record stride and indexed/native references. Name pointer +0 is three bytes; experience +$23 is four bytes, money +$27 two bytes and prize chance +$29 one byte. Undocumented fields remain allocated.
; $D1D000-$D1F32D: PRIMARY_TEXT_POINTERS
; 3,002 three-byte packed dialogue pointers.
; Constraint: Packed pointers address the lower half of a ROM bank; compression uses bit 23.
; $D1F32E-$D1F7D4: TEXT_DICTIONARY_INDEXES
; Native digrams, character substitutions, and dictionary offset tables.
; Constraint: Unchanged dictionary entries are required by compressed native text; do not repurpose them.
; $D1FFD4-$D1FFF6: PRIVATE_TEXT_POINTERS
; Ten private dialogue pointers for Horace exit, Dark Forest, Gobi save, and Professor exchanges, with five intervening reserved bytes.
; Constraint: Pointers start at FFD4, FFD9, FFDC, FFDF, FFE2, FFE5, FFEB, FFEE, FFF1, and FFF4 in bank D1. Preserve gaps FFD7-FFD8 and FFE8-FFEA. Primary-table validation alone does not cover these callers.
; $D28000-$D2801A: NATIVE_SCRIPT_DIRECTORY
; Native script directory header and offsets to callable/helper tables.
; Constraint: Resolve offsets relative to this bank; header bytes are needed even where no source write exists.
; $D2990B-$D29955: GLOBAL_EVENT_HELPER_POINTERS
; Callable global event helpers $00-$18, including dialogue and native save routing.
; Constraint: Preserve helper signatures and shared save helpers $4E/$4F at their separate native call routes.
; $F00000-$F00FFF: INPUT_RING_HELPERS
; Input, Ring-menu, charge, and related gameplay helpers.
; Constraint: Gaps between defined routines remain unverified capacity; keep multiplayer and native return conventions.
; $F01000-$F0FBE0: PYRAMID_MAP_DATA
; Pyramid symbol/map data.
; Constraint: Treat this entire data footprint as a map resource, not executable code or unused space.
; $F10000-$F17FFF: AUXILIARY_DIALOGUE
; Mixed lower-bank storage: additional/contextual dialogue and enemy-prize code/table.
; Constraint: Raw text uses the lower bank half; preserve nested enemy-prize allocations. Resolve private dialogue through its D1 pointer fields, including variants stored in other chapter/area pools. Unclassified gaps are not certified free.
